course: dictionary
lesson: 14902
title: The word recumbent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Recumbent is a formal word, so you may find it in old stories or on a museum sign. Its context often gives the meaning away. «The old man was recumbent on the sofa, resting his eyes.» He is resting on the sofa with his eyes closed, so recumbent means lying down.
explain: Recumbent can also name a special bike. A recumbent bike has a low seat with a back rest, and the rider's legs stretch out in front. «Maya rode her recumbent bike to the park.» Low seat and back rest are the clues: this is a bike you sit back on, not a tall bike you sit up on.
explain: Always check by swapping in a simple word. «The old man was lying down on the sofa, resting his eyes» still makes sense, so recumbent means lying down. If the sentence still works with your meaning, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Recumbent means lying down, especially on your back, or leaning back.
fact: Recumbent is a formal word, so you will often meet it in books and on signs rather than in everyday talk.
fact: A recumbent bicycle has a low seat with a back rest, and the rider's legs go out in front.
fact: In a phrase like «recumbent figure», the word describes a statue of someone lying down, often on a tomb.
fact: Recumbent is also short for a recumbent bicycle: «I bought a recumbent last week.»
exercise: «The cat was recumbent in the sunny window, fast asleep.» What does recumbent mean here? | Standing up tall | Running fast | *Lying down | Hiding under the bed
exercise: «Sam rode his recumbent to school, with his legs stretched out in front.» What is a recumbent? | A kind of bus | A tall bike with high handlebars | A type of helmet | *A low bike with a back rest
exercise: «The statue showed a recumbent knight on the tomb.» Find and copy the word that means lying down. | knight | showed | *recumbent | tomb
test: «Grandad liked to read in a recumbent position on the sofa.» What does recumbent position mean? | Sitting up very straight at a desk | Walking slowly around the room | Standing at the door | *Lying back or lying down
test: Which is true of a recumbent bike? | It has no wheels | You sit upright on a high saddle | It is only for young children | *You sit low with a back rest and your legs in front
exam: In «the recumbent figure of a stone king», what does recumbent describe? | A king walking through a garden | *A figure lying down | A king riding a horse | A bird on a tall tower
